<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Eng wins Y20 bln Thai chemical plant order.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Eng wins Y20 bln Thai chemical plant order.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Engineering &amp; Shipbuilding Co Ltd said on Monday it had received a turn-key order from Siam Mitsui PTA Co Ltd for the construction of a purified terephthalic acid (PTA) plant in Thailand.</p>
<p>The value of the order is about 20 billion yen, Mitsui Engineering said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant, to be built in Rayong, southeast of Bangkok, would have a production capacity of 350,000 tonnes of PTA a year, Mitsui Engineering said. The plant is expected to be completed in May 1998, it said. PTA is used to make polyester and other plastics products.  </p>
<p>Siam Mitsui is a venture formed by a company in the Siam Cement group and Mitsui Petrochemical Industries Ltd.</p>
</text>
